 6. 🤖 Women are missing out on the AI jobs boom 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: LinkedIn. Table: Danielle Alberti/Axios Women made up just over a quarter of U.S. hires for AI roles last year — compared with half of new hires in non-AI occupations, Axios' Emily Peck writes from LinkedIn data out this morning. 

 Men accounted for 74% and women 26% of hires for AI roles in 2025. The highest-paying roles typically have higher percentages of men. Keep reading ... Get Axios Markets . 

 
 
