 7. 🎒 Kindergarten vaccine rates drop 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Vaccination rates among American kindergartners fell during the 2025–2026 school year, Axios' Adriel Bettelheim and Tina Reed write from new CDC data . 

 Exemptions from one or more vaccines increased in 41 states and D.C., growing nationally to 4.2% from 3.6% the year before. Why it matters: The dropoff coincided with the Trump administration's controversial vaccine policy changes and measles cases hitting levels not seen in more than three decades.

