 8. 🛟 1 for the road: Life-saving reunion 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Manuel Balce Ceneta/AP 16-year-old lifeguard Ryder Williams and Nathaniel Rai, the 10-year-old boy he rescued off the coast of California last month, were reunited yesterday in the Oval Office.

 President Trump told them: "What you did was incredible, and everybody saw it," referring to a viral video of the July rescue in Santa Cruz. "When I first saw it, I said, 'roll that back, I want to see that again,'" Trump added. The boys' families joined the Oval Office reunion, along with lifeguard Aaron Bohnen, who aided in the Santa Cruz rescue.

